{"index": 52, "type": "AIMessage", "content": "## Summary\n\n**Incident diagnosed and resolved.**\n\n### Root Cause\n\nThe `orders-api` service acts as a proxy/gateway to the `catalog` backend. Two issues were found:\n\n1. **Proxy timeout too short:** `dependency_timeout_ms` was set to **150ms** in the `orders-api` configuration, but the upstream `catalog` service had an artificial **900ms delay** (`delay_ms`). Since the proxy closes the connection if the upstream doesn't transmit within the timeout, every request would timeout — causing the **502 Bad Gateway** errors observed in the business probe.\n\n2. **Catalog latency too high:** Even with a correct timeout, the catalog's 900ms delay would push the end-to-end response above the **600ms SLO** for request latency.\n\n### Changes Made\n\n| Change | Service | Source | Key | Old Value | New Value |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Increase proxy timeout | `orders-api` | `service-config` | `dependency_timeout_ms` | 150 | 5000 |\n| Reduce backend delay | `catalog` | `dependency-config` | `delay_ms` | 900 | 300 |\n\n### Verification\n\n- **Business probe:** Returns `200 OK` with **~318ms latency** (well below the 600ms SLO).\n- **Underlying fault resolved:** The catalog dependency responds in ~300ms, well within the 5000ms timeout.\n- **Persistence across restart:** After restarting `orders-api`, the config changes persist and the business operation remains healthy.", "tool_calls": []}
